meta {
  name: Sync Exchange Ids
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/siteadmin/tenants/sync-exchange-ids
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{siteAdminToken}}
}

docs {
  Assign a stable integer `exchangeTenantId` to every tenant that is missing one,
  so the external Exchange server can continue per-tenant message/notification
  counts (it keys counts on the integer `peer_tenant_id`). SiteAdmin only —
  requires `system:config` (super_owner). No request body.

  Behaviour (single transaction, idempotent):
  - Seeds the global counter to
    `GREATEST(counter, MAX(legacyTenantId), MAX(exchangeTenantId))`.
  - Migrated tenants (a `legacyTenantId` is present) get
    `exchangeTenantId = legacyTenantId` — their id is never invented.
  - Native tenants (no `legacyTenantId`) get the next value in the sequence,
    starting at `MAX(legacyTenantId) + 1`.
  - Existing `exchangeTenantId` values are NEVER changed; only NULL rows are
    touched. Safe to call repeatedly — a second call is a no-op.

  This is the callable equivalent of the `pnpm sync:tenant-exchange-id` script.
  Run it once after migrating tenants; new tenants get their id automatically on
  create, so routine use is not required.

  Returns in `data`:
  - `floor` — the high-water mark the counter was seeded to.
  - `migrated` — count of migrated tenants whose id was mirrored from legacy.
  - `native` — count of native tenants that received a freshly-allocated id.
}
